      "id": 1,
      "text": "Frankfort began as Oldtown, laid out in 1816, and kept that name until 1834 when it was renamed Frankfort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankfort%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village incorporated in 1827, making it one of Ohio’s oldest communities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankfort%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1972, locals met at the Nordsell home to form the Frankfort Area Historical Society, publishing its first newsletter that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://frankforthistoricalsociety.org/frankfort-area-historical-society-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The FAHS plaque program tells the stories of historic buildings, from the 1885 Citizen’s Bank to the 1855 first hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://frankforthistoricalsociety.org/frankfort-area-historical-society-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1994 grassroots campaign saved Frankfort’s original water tower from demolition, sparking the creation of the Preservation Foundation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
